 **                                                                           **
 **           Bethe Salpeter equation (BSE) for excitation energies           **
 **                solved with Tamm-Dancoff approximation (TDA)               **
 **                                                                           **
 *******************************************************************************
  
 BSE| No cutoff given for occupied orbitals
 BSE| No cutoff given for empty orbitals
 BSE| First occupied index                                                     1
 BSE| Last empty index (not MO index!)                                        22
 BSE| Energy of first occupied index [eV]                               -424.261
 BSE| Energy of last empty index [eV]                                     89.016
 BSE| Energy difference of first occupied index to HOMO [eV]             413.569
 BSE| Energy difference of last empty index to LUMO [eV]                  91.818
 BSE| Number of GW-corrected occupied MOs                                      6
 BSE| Number of GW-corrected empty MOs                                        22
 BSE|
 BSE| No truncation of BSE matrices applied
 BSE|
 BSE| Total peak memory estimate from BSE [GB]                         2.596E-04
 BSE| Peak memory estimate per MPI rank from BSE [GB]                      0.000
 BSE|
 BSE| Diagonalizing A. This will take around 0.E+00 s.
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| **************************************************************************
 BSE| *   Bethe Salpeter equation (BSE) with Tamm Dancoff approximation (TDA)  *
 BSE| **************************************************************************
 BSE|
 BSE| The excitations are calculated by diagonalizing the BSE within the TDA:
 BSE|
 BSE|                       A X^n = Ω^n X^n
 BSE|
 BSE| i.e. in index notation:
 BSE|
 BSE| sum_jb ( A_ia,jb   X_jb^n ) = Ω^n X_ia^n
 BSE|
 BSE| prelim Ref.: Eq. (36) with B=0
 BSE| in PRB 92,045209 (2015); http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.92.045209 .
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| i,j:       occupied molecular orbitals, i.e. state in          [   1,   6]
 BSE| a,b:       unoccupied molecular orbitals, i.e. state in        [   7,  28]
 BSE| n:         Excitation index
 BSE|
 BSE| A_ia,jb = (ε_a-ε_i) δ_ij δ_ab + α * v_ia,jb - W_ij,ab
 BSE|
 BSE| ε_...:                 GW quasiparticle energy
 BSE| δ_...:                 Kronecker delta
 BSE| α:                     spin-dependent factor
 BSE| v_...:                 Electron-hole exchange interaction
 BSE| W_... = 1/ϵ v_...:     Direct interaction screened by 
 BSE|                        dielectric function ϵ(ω=0)
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| The spin-dependent factor is for the requested Singlet is α = 2.0
 BSE|
 BSE| Excitation energies from solving the BSE within the TDA:
 BSE|
